2026-08-29 00:31:20 | INFO     | p2p_knowledge_hub.chunking.recursive_chunker:chunk:54 | Following chunks were produced. [DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d701b062-d9ce-4be4-a32f-017deeab80da'), chunk_index=1, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606201, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 1 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\nSTANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE:\n7.0 INVOICING\nThis procedure is in accordance with Procurement and Payment Policy 20.1.11.\nIntroduction\nUPS is responsible for processing the payment of invoices to suppliers in compliance with university', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3168270a-5946-4705-97b2-d8120aff2e45'), chunk_index=2, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606217, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='policies and procedures. When suppliers provide a Valid Invoice(s), UPS will begin the invoicing process.\nProcedure Outline\n7.1 Invoice Intake\n7.2 Invoice Review and Validation\n7.3 Invoice Processing\n7.4 Invoices with Special Considerations\n7.5 Approved and Completed Invoices\nDefinition\nAccounts Payable Expeditor: Second tier AP processor with advanced roles and responsibilities who\nhandles problem invoice queues and advises a team of processors on issues.', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('973d8f5d-2d21-4e72-8335-7172125481da'), chunk_index=3, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606222, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Accounts Payable Processor: First tier Accounts Payable Processor who processes invoices for payment.\nDetailed Manual Entry: Option to view the invoice in more detail in RU Marketplace. This allows the AP\nprocessor to match the invoice to the purchase order and find possible discrepancies. This view is only\navailable to AP.\nDigital Mail Room (DMR): An automated incoming digital mail program that extracts and validates', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b2ef6cc6-3953-4438-93c6-b5ad66083c4c'), chunk_index=4, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606227, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='supplier invoice data for integration in RU Marketplace.\nE-Invoicing: The preferred method of supplier invoice submission.  Two options include 1) cXML\nwhere suppliers send invoice files via cXML format to Jaggaer directly, 2) Portal Invoicing where\nsuppliers log in to the Rutgers Jaggaer Portal to convert purchase orders to Invoices.\nInternal Purchase Order (IPO): An IPO is a purchase order for a good or service that is provided by a', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d37e0c44-2a20-4045-a504-b2a7325c4611'), chunk_index=5, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606231, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='university unit to another university unit. Related costs are billed to the receiving unit using an approved\nrecharge rate.  UPS generally does not assist with these transactions, except in the event of a change\norder.\nOptical Character Recognition (OCR): Used to populate fields in invoice template.', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('984f99ab-50f3-461b-afeb-4a2055f20258'), chunk_index=6, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606340, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 2 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\nOracle: A database that manages and processes financial data across wide and local area networks. The\nOracle database has its own network component to allow communications across networks. This is the', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4516d7db-47b9-4433-82f8-aef07237ce1c'), chunk_index=7, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606345, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='general ledger system that payments are issued from.\nPunchout Supplier: A preferred supplier set up through UPS for users to procure products by accessing\ntheir catalog through the RU Marketplace portal.  These suppliers are linked on the homepage for easy\naccess.\nPurchase Order (PO) – An official document that Rutgers sends to suppliers to document the sale of\nproducts and services.', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9eb8a375-d8b6-447f-94dc-298e90e1eef1'), chunk_index=8, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606349, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='RU Marketplace: RU Marketplace is the university online system that covers all stages of the procure-to-\npay process excluding payments. This system provides a comprehensive approach to the provider and\nunit. The tool also allows for data analytics by measuring the effectiveness of contracts, transaction\napproval cycle times, and use of automated invoice processing.\nStandard Operational Procedure (SOP): A controlled document that functionally describes the key\nprocedures.', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6f92dde7-55c6-4b85-b7f6-78ed5c7b3bef'), chunk_index=9, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606353, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Unit/Division/Org (UDO): A unit’s 10-segment ledger string used for charging expenses.\nProcedures\n7.1 Invoice Intake\nThe invoicing process begins when a supplier submits an invoice, referencing a valid university purchase\norder (PO) number, allowing Accounts Payable within UPS to process the payment in the RU\nMarketplace  system.   Rutgers accepts a variety of invoice submission types. These are agreed upon\nduring the supplier set up:\n•\ncXML\n•\nSupplier Portal\n•', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('11ae5fc8-c3bc-446d-9ca1-0b6230ab8859'), chunk_index=10, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606357, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='PDF\ncXML Invoicing\ncXML Invoicing is an electronic feed of an invoice that is available to our punchout catalog suppliers.\ncXML invoicing is automatically submitted by the supplier after a good is shipped.  These invoices are\nautomatically processed.\nSupplier Portal Invoicing\nThese suppliers are manually invited to the Jaggaer supplier portal via our eTeam and are provided an', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6d3358f0-c990-41e3-b3e9-87b195c4084b'), chunk_index=11, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606361, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoices submission guide upon registration.  A valid PO must be used in order to submit the invoice.\nOnce it is time to invoice, a supplier will log in to the portal, find their PO and convert this to an invoice.', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9728bdc0-56ad-4d26-a72e-86c93935b01b'), chunk_index=12, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606474, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 3 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\nPDF Invoicing\nFor PDF invoice submission, Suppliers are instructed on the PO to send their invoices to Accounts\nPayable at accountspayable@finance.rutgers.edu.  It is strongly encouraged that invoices be sent via', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5a81a1ea-1d18-478f-89b0-d7acf379dcc5'), chunk_index=13, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606479, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='email, preferably as a PDF file attachment, for quicker processing.  If a vendor is unable to email their\ninvoice, they can mail it directly to Rutgers University, PO Box 3207, Scranton, PA 18505.  Paper invoices\nshould not be sent to any other address at Rutgers.  All mail received at UPS is forwarded to the DMR at\nthe above address.', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cc194f47-c844-4742-a5af-ed10eecb7ed3'), chunk_index=14, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606483, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Any invoice not referencing a university-issued PO cannot be not processed for payment.  Invoices that\nare attached as back-up documentation to PO requisitions are not acceptable for payment, as this is in\nviolation of UPS Policy. In addition, UPS does not review POs for attached invoices, as this is also a\nviolation. Therefore, units should not order or receive goods/services without a valid PO issued prior to', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('017be539-5425-4b64-9a71-8735bdddf999'), chunk_index=15, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606486, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='receipt of said goods/services.  Invoices must be sent through one of the preferred methods noted\nabove. For internal control purposes, the following documents are not considered valid or acceptable\nfor processing and are therefore discarded:\n•\nStatements\n•\nEstimates/proposals/quotations\n•\nAcknowledgements/delivery tickets/packing lists\n•\nAltered invoices\n•\nProforma invoices\n7.2\nInvoice Review and Validation\nInvoices are routed to the Digital Mail Room (DMR) for automated validation and then integrated into', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9baea7ff-fea5-4534-bd89-021c8f7496bd'), chunk_index=16, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606490, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='RU Marketplace.  These automated systems use OCR to review the following requirements:\n• Purchase order number\n• Supplier name as shown on purchase order\n• Invoice that corresponds to an open purchase order\n• Invoice number\n• Invoice date is the same as or later than purchase order date\n• Payment terms\n• Rutgers University as the “Bill To”\n• Supplier “Remit To” address\n• Billing details', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8349e477-3642-49d1-a6bb-ee7d3dcb927f'), chunk_index=17, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606494, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='• Line detail to enable purchase order line matching\nDigital Mail Room –If an invoice is found to be invalid or missing required fields, it is returned to the\nDMR Portal for AP review (exception- if there is an invalid/missing PO, the invoice is auto-rejected by the\nDMR with a message stating such).', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('78ea8773-7174-429a-9d3b-dc1ec591bb8f'), chunk_index=18, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606609, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 4 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n7.3\nInvoice Processing\nUPS has subgroups of invoice processors and expeditors who are tasked with handling invoices for\npayment processing, using RU Marketplace queues where invoices are routinely integrated through', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c11af7e4-4c9c-4b1a-80ac-439e85275eda'), chunk_index=19, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606613, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='DMR or routed after invoice approval and matching processes.\nBelow are relevant queues that can be sorted and filtered to maximize processing:\n•\nInvoice Import Approval – This is a general queue where all validated invoices are routed,\naccessible to all invoice processors and expeditors.\no Suppliers by alphabet (including numeric) queues – These queues are filtered from\nInvoice Import Approval for responsible processor groups.\n•', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0ac8e647-f6f1-4219-9639-8b26bbaa4a36'), chunk_index=20, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606617, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoice Import Notification – Imported invoices may have errors when transmitted to RU\nMarketplace, such as duplicate invoices or invalid purchase orders.  In this queue, only\nprocessors can make the necessary adjustments to the invoices in the interface and push them\nto the general Invoice Import Approval queue when ready for processing.\n•\nMatching Exceptions – Tolerances are allowable variances between an invoice and a purchase', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7215a6c5-10ae-4536-a531-8cf36a475167'), chunk_index=21, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606621, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='order, such as very low dollar amounts.  In many cases, UPS will approve an invoice if a variance\nis small and does not significantly impact a unit’s purchase order funding.  Matching exceptions\nare generated by the system when the variance is beyond allowable tolerances. The expeditor\nmust review before processing can be completed.\n•\nClosed Purchase Order Exceptions – Invoices cannot be processed against a closed or canceled', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5f41319f-a3db-4b1a-a962-7817a1d1ac4b'), chunk_index=22, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606625, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='blanket purchase order or closed or canceled lines on a quantity-based purchase order.  Action\ncannot be taken on a canceled purchase order or line. The expeditor must review before\nprocessing can be completed.\n•\nAccounts Payable Prepayment Review – Only expeditors handle prepayment requests and have\naccess to this queue. This is where unit requisitions via the Pre-Payment Request Form are\nrouted to.\n•', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dad39776-e8dd-484a-a352-e9516a62f0b8'), chunk_index=23, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606628, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Wire Invoice Processing Review and Approval – Invoices with a request to use a wire transfer\nfor the payment method are handled by expeditors, supervisors, or managers.  Domestic wires\nare only done with the approval of the Treasury Department.\nRU Marketplace provides a number of invoice statuses available for units’ viewing. It is important to', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('313b2a4b-deed-4814-b3e6-acb927f1d5bb'), chunk_index=24, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606632, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='understand the status of an invoice in RU Marketplace.  This information is visible to the unit under the\n“Invoice tab”.  If the unit has additional questions, they may contact the University Procurement\nServices Help Desk.\nListed below are the invoice statuses:', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ee99c804-9037-426b-8b7d-79e3fc96e525'), chunk_index=25, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606745, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 5 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n• In Process - An invoice with “In Process” status is ready for an AP processor to initiate the', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('de627037-6f24-4267-a2fb-86174d1f4843'), chunk_index=26, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606749, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='payment process (as long as the invoice is under $5K and is not a sub-award nor an invoice in the\nexception queue).\n• Payable - An invoice with “Payable” status has been completely processed through invoicing and\nis in queue for payment to be issued per terms. This means that an invoice will reside in the\nsystem with “Payable” status until payment is issued according to the contract terms.', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('58ed2a56-5cbc-429c-a498-228ebf85551a'), chunk_index=27, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606753, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='• Paid - An invoice with “Paid” status has been paid per terms, and payment information is\navailable from Oracle and RU Marketplace.\n• Canceled - An invoice with “Canceled” status has been canceled by UPS for reasons such as\nfinding duplicate invoices.  In addition, a unit may reach out to UPS and request an invoice be', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d6091c70-c830-4bdc-ae2d-d49f8347550f'), chunk_index=28, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606757, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='canceled if they know it was issued incorrectly, such as from a dispute.  Canceled invoices are\nedited with an X, XX, etc. to differentiate with the true valid invoice that should be processed.\nFor example, a duplicate would be marked “INV1982X” and “INV1982” would be paid.  Once\ncanceled, an invoice cannot be processed unless resubmitted with an unique invoice number.\n7.3.1\nInvoice Review, Adjusting, and Completing', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3dc9f53b-81c5-4658-866d-e56c0d79cac9'), chunk_index=29, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606760, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Accounts Payable processes invoices when the processor accesses their designated alphabet queue,\nsorts the invoices by invoices over $5K first and then by folder entry date (oldest first) and carefully\nverifies the amounts.\nThree different screens are opened in RU Marketplace order to review line by line:\n1) The invoice in “Detailed Manual Entry” view in the interface.\n2) The scanned image of the invoice (via DMR, etc.).', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('38b6f2c4-2f01-4c7a-ae79-6cfa3b28539c'), chunk_index=30, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606764, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3) The purchase order referenced on the invoice.\nThe requirements for invoices on the invoice interface must be matched exactly to the corresponding\ninformation on the supplier invoice image.  This is another check for accuracy.  The processor can make\nadjustments directly on the interface.  For example, if a supplier address is not captured correctly\nthrough validation, the processor can correct that field.', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b1069b03-0dd3-40fe-94c5-c17370d045e2'), chunk_index=31, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606768, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The processor then compares the corrected invoice and the purchase order, checking that all\nrequirements for invoices (date, remit to address, invoice number, etc.) accurately match. The invoice is\nreviewed for discrepancies and adjustments can be made on the amount or quantity, line by line where\napplicable, within tolerances (See 7.3.2 Invoice Matching and Resolution).\nCommon issues may surface during review and can be resolved before completing the invoicing process:', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('602c0880-6900-42ab-875e-c786aecdb592'), chunk_index=32, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606877, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 6 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n•\nThe purchase order or a line has insufficient funds. Accounts Payable can contact the unit via the\nComments tab and request an order modification. This is done through the PO Modification', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3bc1a924-756f-4f8d-a1ce-d4da72f11b17'), chunk_index=33, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606882, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='form in RU Marketplace.  Units are responsible for ensuring that their purchase order has\nsufficient funds.  In some cases, a new purchase order may be needed to apply to an invoice for\npayment.  The new purchase order should reference the old purchase order to assist in resolving\nany issues.\n•\nInvoice disputes arise when a supplier invoices the unit for items that either do not match the', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('575d041e-66e7-4e00-88a7-74a59989b3a7'), chunk_index=34, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606886, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='items requested on the purchase order, or the goods/services delivered to the unit are not\ncorrect.  Units are responsible for resolving invoice disputes with the supplier and will notify\nAccounts Payable if invoice processing can continue as needed.\n•\nInternal supplier invoices can also come through RU Marketplace queues to Accounts Payable.\nIf an invoice does not match an internal purchase order (IPO), an expeditor may contact the', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2a132b3e-8fcb-4471-885a-7fea6ef91b2e'), chunk_index=35, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606890, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='internal units for resolution, particularly for high dollar amounts.\n•\nElectronic invoices from punchout supplier file transfers may not be matched to a purchase\norder.  Accounts Payable may reach out to the supplier for resolution.\n•\nNon-standard invoices may require a different process for payment and accounting purposes\noutside of RU Marketplace.  See 8.0 Payments.', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b8a3ba9c-1275-4032-9956-e7825add587d'), chunk_index=36, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606894, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When all required fields match on the invoice and purchase order, the processor completes the process\nfrom the interface.  This will change the invoice status to “Payable” and move it to a system queue for\npayment.\n7.3.2 Invoice Matching and Resolution\nInvoices are subject to an internal system matching process once they are fully accounted for by a\nprocessor.  This process may generate exceptions and route invoices to exception queues.', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('15752f16-69ae-4189-bea9-241d46bd7cdd'), chunk_index=37, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606897, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The two most common exceptions:\n• Matching Exceptions, which apply to open purchase orders\n• Closed Purchase Order Exceptions, which apply to closed or partially closed purchase orders\nTolerance Thresholds\nMarketplace has built-in tolerance thresholds that prevent invoices from exceeding the purchase order\namount without AP review. These tolerance thresholds are designed to allow for incidental expenses', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('217ce378-05ea-436b-b4f7-50a5309b6afa'), chunk_index=38, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 606901, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='that may not have been quoted when the PO was established. Examples include: setup charges,\nmailing/shipping expenses etc. Reasonable expenses applying these tolerances may be approved by the\nAP Associate Director.  They are not intended for offsetting PO overages (more Goods Delivered that the\nPurchase Order stated).', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cbca0072-6685-4bb0-b357-33886f9d106f'), chunk_index=39, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607023, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 7 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\nAccounts Payable expeditors are responsible for researching and resolving these invoice issues.  The unit\ncan be contacted for resolution assistance.  The unit must update Accounts Payable via the Comments', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d2f49fb2-dfb7-4e5e-9cd4-f8ffdfb1fcd3'), chunk_index=40, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607028, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tab in RU Marketplace if they are taking action.  It is critical that the unit selects the specific\nexpeditor/processor’s name on the interface to notify them of any change.  Until action is taken to\ncomplete processing, invoices will remain in these exception queues.\n• Matching Exceptions – A matching exception occurs when the invoice overbills the PO by', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8d8a06cc-ed2d-44cb-a559-a4437603ccc0'), chunk_index=41, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607031, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='quantity or amount. Usually the unit would have to take action per the request of Accounts\nPayable, such as doing an order modification on the purchase order.\nTypes of Closed Purchase Order Exceptions:\n• Closed Purchase Order – The purchase order has been fully expended and auto-closed during\ninvoice processing.\n• Canceled Purchase Order – The unit can request a purchase order to be canceled by UPS using a', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f9a87d56-64b7-43cd-acc0-060252221fbc'), chunk_index=42, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607035, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='PO modification form.  This action not only closes the purchase order, but also returns the\nencumbered funds back to the UDO\n• Closed Line – A specific line on a purchase order can be fully expended and consequently closed.\nHowever, this does not mean the full purchase order is closed, and other lines may be open for\ninvoice processing.', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7d9e837c-e653-462b-99ed-40f054760868'), chunk_index=43, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607039, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='• Canceled line – A specific line on a quantity-based purchase order has been canceled as\nrequested by the unit using a Change Order form.  The line would be closed and encumbered funds\nwould be returned to the UDO.\n7.4\nInvoices with Special Considerations\nAccounts Payable may receive other types of invoices for processing. These invoices result when there is', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f0aa1ad6-c44f-40b0-b219-5b61745dd1ff'), chunk_index=44, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607043, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='a need to process a credit to Rutgers, recurring payments, pre-payments or invoices that fall outside the\ngeneral invoicing structure, amongst others.\n• Credit Memos – Credit memos are issued by the supplier to return funds owed to the University,\ngenerated from duplicate payments, overpayments, or incorrectly issued payments. They will be\nscanned and validated through DMR and go through the regular invoicing process in RU', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8f8cb14-5c6f-4f91-bbc2-b7f29c8ea395'), chunk_index=45, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607047, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Marketplace, including routing to exception queues.  A purchase order must be open in order for\na credit to be processed against it.  Accounts Payable may re-open a closed purchase order or line\nin RU Marketplace and Finance Management in order to apply owed funds to the purchase order\nand the UDO.\n• Invoices $5,000 and over and all subawards– Invoices $5,000 and over and all subawards require', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f746b4af-c1d2-4bbc-80da-134fa9149e40'), chunk_index=46, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607050, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='online approval in RU Marketplace based on the unit’s approval hierarchy.  See Approve an\nInvoice.\nTo process an invoice $5,000 and over and subawards:\n1) The invoice goes into a queue for Invoice Review/Approval.', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f12939fa-0706-47f0-adc6-1c0f876ba777'), chunk_index=47, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607163, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 8 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n2) The system recognizes when the amount of a processed invoice is $5,000 and over and\nsubawards and sends the designated unit approver a notification to take action.', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3934f630-1c55-4d2b-8040-df779958db80'), chunk_index=48, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607168, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3) The unit approver must open the invoice and approve it from their actions menu. Until\nthis is done, the invoice remains with “In Process” status and cannot route for payment.\nThe expense is not reflected in Oracle until the invoice is approved in RU Marketplace.\n4) Additionally, any invoice valued at $1M or greater shall be approved at the invoice level by', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('955264a9-7129-47e2-8d71-99c36dcaa508'), chunk_index=49, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607171, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the Executive Vice President-Chief Financial Officer and University Treasurer and, in\naddition, by any one (1) of the following University Officers: the Chair of the Board of\nGovernors, President, Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs, Executive Vice\nPresident for Strategic Planning and Operations and Executive Vice President- Chief\nOperating Officer, or Secretary of the University\n5) Once online approval is complete, the invoice changes to “Payable” status, and is passed', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fafb5412-04ab-4468-aca1-d4d636b2d4c7'), chunk_index=50, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607175, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='to Oracle for further validation for accounting/payment.  Payment is issued in Oracle\nbased on invoice due date and supplier terms.\n6) Accounts Payable runs weekly clean-up reports to identify invoices still requiring online\napproval from the unit. Designated approvers and business managers are contacted to\ntake action.  This helps accounting processes to post expenses in appropriate open\nperiods.  In cases when the designated approver has changed, Accounts Payable could', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c2c231e8-f01b-45b4-8362-09f531974f5a'), chunk_index=51, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607179, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='forward the invoice to the new authorized approver so that they may see approval actions\nin RU Marketplace.  If an approver has permanently changed, the unit should contact the\nUPS Help Desk to update the approver information.\n• Pre-payments – Pre-payments are payments that a supplier may need before the goods or\nservices are delivered, such as a deposit to start work on a project. The supplier must provide an', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('91db6c46-a1e2-418e-a5eb-297b4c40877a'), chunk_index=52, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607182, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoice which should be attached to the pre-payment request. These payments have immediate\npayment terms and Accounts Payable expeditors process pre-payments as acknowledgements to\nthe unit that their request is acceptable.  See Pre-Payment Request Process Instructions.\nTo initiate a pre-payment:\n1) In RU Marketplace, the unit will complete the pre-payment request under\nForms/Supplemental Forms. The request must include a valid a purchase order number.', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1217a485-281a-4224-a525-9e9b24d7691a'), chunk_index=53, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607186, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2) The requisitions will route to the AP Prepayment Review Queue, where expeditors review.\nPre-payment terms must be reflected on the contract or the supplier’s invoice to constitute\na valid pre-payment. If they do not qualify, the requisition will be rejected and the invoice\nmust submitted thru the normal channels.', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('110c2de3-7337-48c2-8019-d58c894c6cbe'), chunk_index=54, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607284, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 9 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n•\nSmall Businesses – Some suppliers are small businesses and by nature may not be equipped\nto produce generic invoices that would be valid for Accounts Payable processing.  (e.g. A local', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('48a1f1b6-90ce-4b7a-b9c6-49c5070197bf'), chunk_index=55, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607288, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='pizza store may issue a handwritten receipt without an invoice number). An invoice processor\ncan then add an invoice number following a naming convention when processing in the\ninterface.  Additionally, small businesses depend heavily on quick payments, therefore\npayment terms can be adjusted as needed.\n•\nUtilities – Some regularly recurring invoices for utilities, (e.g. PSE&G, municipal water) can go', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('acec4a5e-6764-477f-a740-80927089dfd2'), chunk_index=56, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607292, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='through a purchase order or a Check Request. Utility payment terms are immediate.\n•\nWire Transfers – A wire transfer is an electronic payment for an invoice that has been\nsubmitted for processing.  Wire payments are only for international payments. Accounts\nPayable processes invoices with wire transfer forms with the assistance of University\nTreasury. All domestic wires must be approved by the Treasury Department. Selection of', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f82acb79-75a8-421c-a16d-348babb474d9'), chunk_index=57, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607296, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='wire payment does not initiate a wire payment.  The appropriate wire requisition form must\nbe completed.\nTo initiate a wire transfer payment:\n1) The domestic or international wire form can be found in the form repository in RU\nMarketplace and is routed to the Wire Review Approval Queue for an AP Expeditor,\nSupervisor, or Manager to sort and review by date submitted.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3de3e8ee-b713-4e11-adca-1f3c671411fa'), chunk_index=58, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607299, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2) The AP Expeditor reviews the requisition to ensure the following items have been provided\nor that the invoice has not been paid before approving:\n•\nA valid purchase order number\n•\nMatching invoice amount between the attached back up documentation and the requisition\n•\nConfirmation that the invoice has not been paid; Invoice status should show as “In Process”.\nOnce confirmed, the requisition is forwarded to University Treasury', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0ac0d0ee-c380-4ed0-8da9-9607ce2faf7f'), chunk_index=59, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607304, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3) Accounts Payable reviews the request for valid banking information, approves and routes to\nTreasury for their review and processing.\n4) The approved requisition will be routed to the Wire Invoice Processing Approval queue, and\nthen AP will book the expense through RU Marketplace.\n7.5\nApproved and Completed Invoices\nAfter Accounts Payable completes invoice processing, the invoice status changes to “Payable” and is\nqueued for payment.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('849cebb1-3ca6-4c12-882f-4259fb77c2a2'), chunk_index=60, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607376, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='© 2025\nRutgers University Procurement Services\nPage 10 of 10\nCAUTION:  A printed copy of this document is uncontrolled and may not be the current version. Access current version on the UPS website.\n1) An email notification is sent to the Requestor unit indicated as the “Prepared for” on the\nrequisition, or individual to whom the purchase order has been reassigned (owner).  This', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9d8dfebf-04bb-4edf-ad88-6aaff7f1c580'), chunk_index=61, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607381, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='notifies units that their invoice is in process and payment can be expected to issue according to\nterms. If the “Prepared For” field was left blank, the notification is routed to the “Prepared By”\nuser.\n2) System processes run multiple times on a daily basis and invoices with “Payable” status are\nexported by Oracle from RU Marketplace to the Finance Management module.', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cb238c4f-d09a-472b-b0c0-ed1aa02113bb'), chunk_index=62, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607385, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3) Once in Oracle, invoices are in queue for validation.  Daily validation processes are run by the\nsystem, searching and batching according to payment methods and due dates.   Validation can\nalso be run by the Accounts Payable Associate Director for special circumstances.\n4) Payments are issued through Oracle in Finance Management and payment information is\nexported back to RU Marketplace.', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c2884e95-af66-46c1-8555-7361c32d85b2'), chunk_index=63, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607388, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5) The invoice status changes to “Paid” in RU Marketplace.  The payment number routes to RU\nMarketplace from Oracle in batch processing and is located in the Invoice tab. The payment date\ncan be viewed under the Invoice History tab or on the invoice summary screen itself.\nReferences\nCampus Instructions\nInvoice Approval Process Instructions\nApprove an Invoice\nPre-Payment Request Process Instructions\nSubmit a Goods Request\nSubmit a Service Request\nRevisions', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0454d41d-7682-4111-bb67-2bb9e1de6c23'), chunk_index=64, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('7b298a55-666e-400a-98df-c7fa3373d125'), document_group_id=UUID('29afaa7a-b520-462e-ab4f-777c6e04f73e'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 28, 19, 1, 20, 607392, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Effective Date\nApprover\nChange Reference\nIssue #\n06/2023\nM. Gower\n3', page_no=10, section=None, title=None)]
